Asica_en_las_Tuller%C3%ADas_%28National_Gallery%2C_Londres%2C_1862%29.jpg?width=500","image_url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/MANET_-_M%C3%BAsica_en_las_Tuller%C3%ADas_%28National_Gallery%2C_Londres%2C_1862%29.jpg?width=500","person_roles":[],"in_collection":null},{"id":"aw53","title_display":"The Fighting Temeraire","title":"The Fighting Temeraire","title_original":"","work_type":"painting","year":null,"country":"","node_type":"work","is_center":false,"primary_image_url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Turner%2C_J._M._W._-_The_Fighting_T%C3%A9m%C3%A9raire_tugged_to_her_last_Berth_to_be_broken.jpg?width=500","image_url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Turner%2C_J._M._W._-_The_Fighting_T%C3%A9m%C3%A9raire_tugged_to_her_last_Berth_to_be_broken.jpg?width=500","person_roles":[],"in_collection":null},{"id":"aw21","title_display":"Rain, Steam and Speed – The Great Western Railway","title":"Rain, Steam and Speed – The Great Western Railway","title_original":"","work_type":"painting","year":null,"country":"","node_type":"work","is_center":false,"primary_image_url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Turner_-_Rain%2C_Steam_and_Speed_-_National_Gallery_file.jpg?width=500","image_url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Turner_-_Rain%2C_Steam_and_Speed_-_National_Gallery_file.jpg?width=500","person_roles":[],"in_collection":null},{"id":"aw22","title_display":"Beach Scene at Trouville","title":"Beach Scene at Trouville","title_original":"","work_type":"painting","year":null,"country":"","node_type":"work","is_center":false,"primary_image_url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Eug%C3%A8ne_Boudin_-_Sc%C3%A8ne_de_plage_%C3%A0_Trouville.jpg?width=500","image_url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Eug%C3%A8ne_Boudin_-_Sc%C3%A8ne_de_plage_%C3%A0_Trouville.jpg?width=500","person_roles":[{"person_id":"ap6","person_name":"Claude Monet","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Contemporary/Subject"},{"person_id":"ap6","person_name":"Claude Monet","role_type":"collaborator","role_detail":"Protégé"},{"person_id":"ap360","person_name":"Charles Baudelaire","role_type":"collaborator","role_detail":"Advocate"},{"person_id":"ap354","person_name":"Eugène Boudin","role_type":"artist","role_detail":"Artist"},{"person_id":"ap370","person_name":"Parisian Bourgeoisie","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Subject"},{"person_id":"ap369","person_name":"The Parisian Bourgeoisie","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Subject"},{"person_id":"ap356","person_name":"Gustave Courbet","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Subject"},{"person_id":"ap368","person_name":"Paul Durand-Ruel","role_type":"collaborator","role_detail":"Art Dealer"},{"person_id":"ap359","person_name":"Empress Eugénie","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Subject"},{"person_id":"ap355","person_name":"Marie-Anne Guédès","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Subject"}],"in_collection":null}],"edges":[{"source":"aw5","target":"aw108","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"Three years later-Monet applies same principles to figure painting","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw110","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"54 years later-same artist pushes atmospheric dissolution to complete abstraction","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw111","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"Blanche Hoschede learned from the artist who painted this revolutionary work","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw25","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"Whistler's Tonalist works, like this one, share a profound connection with Monet's painting in their mutual focus on atmosphere, mood, and color harmony over precise depiction, leading to similar public controversy.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw91","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"Van Gogh built upon the Impressionist foundation of capturing light's effect on water, but infused it with his signature emotional intensity and symbolic color, demonstrating a lineage of expressive landscape painting.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw92","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"While stylistically different, Rothko's abstract works can be seen as a culmination of the Impressionist project to dematerialize form into pure color and light, focusing entirely on the sensory and emotional experience of perception.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw23","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Like many of his contemporaries, Monet was influenced by Japanese Ukiyo-e woodblock prints. The flattened perspective, unconventional composition, and focus on transient natural phenomena seen in prints by artists like Hokusai are reflected in this work.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw89","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Boudin was Monet's mentor who famously encouraged him to paint outdoors ('en plein air'), directly influencing Monet's method of capturing fleeting moments of light and weather.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw109","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Boudin taught Monet plein air painting 14 years earlier-this is the student surpassing the teacher","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw42","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Manet's radical depiction of modern urban life and his sketchy, seemingly 'unfinished' brushwork broke academic rules and paved the way for Monet to focus on contemporary subjects like an industrial harbor.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw53","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Monet studied Turner's work in London and was deeply influenced by his atmospheric, light-filled maritime scenes and expressive use of color to depict sun and water.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw21","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Turner's atmospheric paintings, which prioritized the effects of light and weather over detail, were a major inspiration for Monet's approach to capturing fleeting moments and industrial scenes.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw5","target":"aw22","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Boudin was Monet's mentor who famously encouraged him to paint outdoors ('en plein air'). Boudin's focus on capturing natural light and skies on the Normandy coast directly shaped Monet's early development.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw110","target":"aw5","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Same artist, 54 years later-from naming a movement to transcending it","direction":"incoming"},{"source":"aw111","target":"aw5","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Grew up with Monet's revolutionary works as her daily environment","direction":"incoming"},{"source":"aw108","target":"aw5","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Three years earlier-same artist, growing ambition","direction":"incoming"},{"source":"aw109","target":"aw5","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"Boudin taught Monet to paint outdoors in 1858-without that moment, no Impressionism","direction":"incoming"}],"lineage":{"influenced_by":["aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5"],"influences":["aw5","aw5","aw5","aw5"]},"stats":{"total_connected":13,"influences_count":7,"influenced_count":10,"filter":"all","vault_count":0,"beyond_count":13}}